I've been curious and had a peek into the code. I am not perfectly sure
but the asymptotic results don't seem to depend on the stack size if
the individual objects don't stack, as in your case with unicorn horns
or ivory rings.

Your wizmode sample size is certainly far too small to deduce anything
serious WRT stack sizes, and the variances in your data above seems to
reflect that quite obviously.

I've written some test code with your luck, cursedness, and stack size
parameters and they roughly match your results (amount and distribution)
in case of every single test-run. Increasing the number of runs to 500
I observed that the results average on 3 skeletons created; and this is
independent of the actual stack size.

